Works well with NumPy

Widely used in Data Science and Machine Learning


Import Pandas

import pandas as pd


---

📌 2. What is a Pandas Series?

A Series is a one-dimensional (1D) labeled array.

import pandas as pd

s = pd.Series([10,20,30,40])

print(s)

Key Point

> Series = 1D labeled data structure




---

📊 3. What is a Pandas DataFrame?

A DataFrame is a two-dimensional (2D) table consisting of rows and columns.

import pandas as pd

data = {
    "Name": ["Ram", "Sita", "John"],
    "Age": [20, 22, 21]
}

df = pd.DataFrame(data)

print(df)

Key Point

> DataFrame = Rows + Columns




---

⚖️ 4. Series vs DataFrame

Series	DataFrame

1D	2D
Usually represents one column	Multiple columns
Simpler	More powerful
Labeled values	Labeled rows and columns



