---

🔀 27. Merge – Combining Tables

merge() combines DataFrames using common columns or keys.


---

Inner Join

Returns only matching records.

pd.merge(
    df1,
    df2,
    on="ID",
    how="inner"
)


---

Left Join

Returns all records from the left DataFrame.

pd.merge(
    df1,
    df2,
    on="ID",
    how="left"
)


---

Right Join

Returns all records from the right DataFrame.

pd.merge(
    df1,
    df2,
    on="ID",
    how="right"
)


---

Outer Join

Returns records from both DataFrames.

pd.merge(
    df1,
    df2,
    on="ID",
    how="outer"
)


---

🔑 28. Index-Based Merging

Using join():

df1.join(df2)

Or using indexes with merge():

pd.merge(
    df1,
    df2,
    left_index=True,
    right_index=True
)


